                <pb facs="0723" n="625" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg625"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Choate.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-12-29"><hi rendition="#italic">December 29,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 522.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 459 of the 19th instant transmitting an order upon Her Majesty’s
                    paymaster-general for £1,000, which the British secretary of war has awarded to
                    Mrs. George F. Labram in recognition of the assistance afforded by her late
                    husband to Her Majesty’s troops at Kimberly.</p>
                <p>The order has this day been forwarded to Mrs. Labram.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
